  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-08-26T10:36:47.410Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "it feels almost wrong to create guns for anything but index, due to using gesture weight, then oculus controllers come around and  have gesture weight as grip instead of trigger for index, making compatibility for all controllers really hard to manage.\n\ni'd think having controller data to add-on-to gestures and gesture-weights like:\n\nTrigger (Float 1-0) If controller's trigger isnt analog (oculus, old vive), set to Bool instead.\n\nGrip (Float 1-0) For Oculus analog, or Index pressure grip, or bool for vive too.\n\nJump (Bool) for detecting jump button pressed, certain actions like for cartoon smoke or hops could be detected without needing Grounded, as many things can lift you up causing the Grounded bool to be tripped, making effects happen when not wanted yet.\n\nthis way avatar creators for guns and like can more reliably get data and feel better as guns or anything, for all\n\ni've had to create a system to detect an index controller grabbing without using gestures, using contacts on ends of the fingers and palm, for example\n\ni tried searching for a post like this but nothing comes up, unfortunately",
